rmw_zenoh_cpp 0.2.10 (ros-jazzy-rmw-zenoh-cpp 0.2.10-1noble.20260902.013751): the lost wake-up in
rmw_wait. check_and_attach_condition() ends with `wait_set_data->triggered = false` while rmw_wait no
longer holds condition_mutex around it (upstream #1005 moved the lock), so a guard condition or a
message that triggers between its attach and that line is forgotten, and a wait with no timeout
sleeps forever: OpenVINS's MultiThreadedExecutor froze 4 of 4 live and 2 of 5 on the zenoh bench
(2026-10-04, scratch/vio_day). This is upstream's own fix, verbatim: ros2/rmw_zenoh PR #1036
(rolling e754341, issue #1032), backported to jazzy as #1040 (254d182) and released in 0.2.11
(2026-09-12). Built by ros/tools/build_rmw_zenoh_fix.sh into ros/build/rmw_zenoh_fix/; the images
COPY that librmw_zenoh_cpp.so over the apt one. AT THE NEXT APT BUMP: at 0.2.11 or later the fix is
in the package and this patch, the script and the COPY lines go; still at 0.2.10, rerun the script
(it refuses an rmw_zenoh_cpp that is not 0.2.10).
diff --git a/rmw_zenoh_cpp/src/rmw_zenoh.cpp b/rmw_zenoh_cpp/src/rmw_zenoh.cpp
index 501ed02..da770df 100644
--- a/rmw_zenoh_cpp/src/rmw_zenoh.cpp
+++ b/rmw_zenoh_cpp/src/rmw_zenoh.cpp
@@ -2091,6 +2091,9 @@ check_and_attach_condition(
   const rmw_events_t * const events,
   rmw_zenoh_cpp::rmw_wait_set_data_t * wait_set_data)
 {
+  // This function runs without wait_set_data->condition_mutex. Taking it here
+  // deadlocks against the producers, so this function must never write
+  // wait_set_data->triggered.
   if (guard_conditions) {
     for (size_t i = 0; i < guard_conditions->guard_condition_count; ++i) {
       rmw_zenoh_cpp::GuardCondition * gc =
@@ -2165,11 +2168,6 @@ check_and_attach_condition(
     }
   }
 
-  // No conditions are available. Set the triggered flag of the wait_set to false.
-  // Note that wait_set_data->condition_mutex has been locked before calling
-  // check_and_attach_condition. So it's safe to modify the wait_set_data triggered flag.
-  wait_set_data->triggered = false;
-
   return false;
 }
 }  // namespace
@@ -2222,7 +2220,7 @@ rmw_wait(
 
   {
     // We explicitly do not lock the condition_mutex here
-    // This is fine, as the attachment returns atomically is a signal was ready
+    // This is fine, as the attachment returns atomically if a signal was ready
     // If anything triggers after that point, wait_set_data->triggered will be set
     // to true under mutex.
     // Note taking the mutex here leads to a deadlock.
